  {
   "id": 10000,
   "type": "MarkdownNote",
   "pos": [
    40,
    110
   ],
   "size": [
    440,
    420
   ],
   "flags": {},
   "order": 0,
   "mode": 0,
   "inputs": [],
   "outputs": [],
   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## 01 \u00b7 Text \u2192 Image (Krea 2 Turbo)\n\n**Write the prompt** in the green *PROMPT* box, in natural sentences.\nDescribe hands explicitly when they matter (\"left hand resting on the cup, relaxed fingers\").\n\n**Enhance prompt?** The LLM (the same Qwen3-VL encoder) expands short prompts. Turn it off for exact control.\n\n**Pipeline:** base 8 steps \u2192 small-FACE detailer \u2192 small-HAND detailer \u2192 SeedVR2 7B 2\u00d7 upscale.\nThe detailers fix only **small** faces and hands (at 2 MP: width < ~270 / ~315 px, see the *Only SMALL\u2026* nodes). Krea 2 already renders large faces perfectly, and re-rendering them only exaggerates skin texture (this was tested).\n\n**Tuning:**\n- Small faces still mushy: raise the face denoise to 0.45. If identity drifts, lower it to 0.25.\n- To force-fix every hand, set max_value to 9999 on the hands filter. Broken hands: denoise 0.5, or use *06 Qwen edit*.\n- To skip the upscale: right-click the orange group \u2192 *Bypass Group Nodes*.\n- Character LoRA: select it in *Character LoRA*, press Ctrl+B to enable, and put the trigger word in the prompt.\n\nLicense: Krea 2 Community License. Commercial use only if your revenue (incl. affiliates) is under $1M, and you must add your own content filter. Details: LICENSING.md in the repo."
   ],
   "color": "#432",
   "bgcolor": "#653",
   "title": "READ ME"
  }
